  "chapter": 715,
  "signer": "ANDREW M. CUOMO",
  "text": "\n \n                APPROVAL MEMORANDUM - No. 62 Chapter 715\n \n        MEMORANDUM filed with Assembly Bill Number 57, entitled:\n \n    \"AN  ACT to amend the general business law, in relation to requiring\n        domestic violence and sexual  assault  awareness  education  for\n        persons  engaged  in  the  practice  of  nail specialty, waxing,\n        natural hair styling, esthetics and cosmetology\"\n \n    APPROVED\n \n  This bill would require those individuals seeking to  become  licensed\nin  the  practices  of  nail  specialty,  waxing,  natural hair styling,\nesthetics, and cosmetology  to  receive  domestic  violence  and  sexual\nassault  awareness  education.  It also requires the Department of State\n(\"Department\") to make such programs available to licensees on a  volun-\ntary basis.\n\n  In  developing these programs, the Department is authorized to consult\nwith a domestic abuse prevention advocacy organization. It would also be\nuseful if the Department were able to  consult  with  a  sexual  assault\nawareness  advocacy  organization. To that end, I have reached an agree-\nment with the Legislature to pass legislation in the upcoming session to\nallow the Department to consult with both  types  of  organizations.  On\nthat basis, I am signing this bill.\n \n  This bill is approved.                      (signed) ANDREW M. CUOMO\n \n                                ______\n",
  "year": 2019
 },
